  "articleSummary": "The article is a practical, tutorial-style guide for self-hosters securing Docker services on home networks or public VPS/cloud platforms, emphasizing that they are responsible for configuration and verification. It covers deliberate image updates and version pinning instead of blindly using `:latest`, secure secret handling with tools such as Docker Secrets, 1Password, Bitwarden, Vault, and AWS Secrets Manager, plus canary tokens, read-only volumes, firewalls, network segmentation, authenticated Nginx proxies, access controls, monitoring, and production checks. The tone is approachable and lightly humorous, framing security as keeping out “the riff-raff” and presenting a menu of techniques readers can choose according to their risk and setup.",
